From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: mixer: Run the H6 display engine at 696 MHz

Scalers produce one pixel per display engine clock cycle, so they need
the clock to be comfortably above the pixel rate during the active part
of each line. With 600 MHz, that doesn't hold for high refresh rate modes
with reduced blanking. 2560x1440@144 (592.5 MHz, 2560 of 2720 pixels
per line active) uses about 93 % of the cycles for an upscaled plane,
which shows up as horizontal stripes. Kodi always upscales its 1080p
user interface to such modes.

Lowering the clock to provoke the same load at 3840x2160@60 shows stripes
at about 90 % and works at 86 %.

The vendor kernel runs the H6 display engine at 696 MHz. Do the same,
which brings the 1440p@144 case down to 80 %.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c
index c85bc5d089dd..5452d89d889c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c
@@ -1165,7 +1165,7 @@ static const struct sun8i_mixer_cfg sun50i_h6_mixer0_cfg = {
 		.scanline_ed	= {2048},
 	},
 	.de_type	= SUN8I_MIXER_DE3,
-	.mod_rate	= 600000000,
+	.mod_rate	= 696000000,
 	.ui_num		= 3,
 	.vi_num		= 1,
 	.has_formatter	= 1,
